{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00102",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.11,
      "end_seconds": 6.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Doctor, if you're free, we can start. I've got the numbers noted down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.57,
      "end_seconds": 11.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Great. Hello, come in and sit down. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 12.62,
      "end_seconds": 17.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "Good morning, um, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.86,
      "end_seconds": 21.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 22.77,
      "end_seconds": 25.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "We came because of burning in both feet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.29,
      "end_seconds": 30.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.27,
      "end_seconds": 34.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "I've had it for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.69,
      "end_seconds": 37.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "I see. Is there anything that triggers it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.12,
      "end_seconds": 42.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "So, uh, bedsheets touching them definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.73,
      "end_seconds": 47.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "How would you describe it, mild, moderate, severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.2,
      "end_seconds": 49.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "It's severe, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.34,
      "end_seconds": 55.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 55.32,
      "end_seconds": 60.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.69,
      "end_seconds": 63.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Alright, later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.77,
      "end_seconds": 74.22,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "I mean, as for numbness in the toes, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.34,
      "end_seconds": 78.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Alright, does it happen all the time or in spells?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.05,
      "end_seconds": 81.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "It comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.07,
      "end_seconds": 84.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "How much is it bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.18,
      "end_seconds": 86.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "It's mild, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.68,
      "end_seconds": 104.26,
      "duration_seconds": 14.58,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.67,
      "end_seconds": 107.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Uh, thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.45,
      "end_seconds": 109.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "Any bladder problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.23,
      "end_seconds": 113.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "So, no bladder problems, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.46,
      "end_seconds": 116.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "And fever, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.39,
      "end_seconds": 121.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "No fever, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 121.7,
      "end_seconds": 125.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.76,
      "end_seconds": 131.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.28,
      "end_seconds": 140.4,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any foot ulcers, back pain or hand symptoms at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.76,
      "end_seconds": 154.49,
      "duration_seconds": 12.73,
      "text": "Uh, no, no foot ulcers, no back pain, no hand symptoms. I was feeling unsteady in the dark at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.9,
      "end_seconds": 156.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.57,
      "end_seconds": 158.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.82,
      "end_seconds": 162.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.13,
      "end_seconds": 164.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 165.78,
      "end_seconds": 175.41,
      "duration_seconds": 9.63,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Blood pressure 123 over 68, temperature is 36.8 degrees. Respiratory rate 17, oxygen saturation is 98 percent, pulse 71."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.52,
      "end_seconds": 180.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Okay, noted. Right, what medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.98,
      "end_seconds": 184.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 186.4,
      "end_seconds": 194.43,
      "duration_seconds": 8.03,
      "text": "Well, doctor, I think the last prescription for the omeprazole was 40 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.61,
      "end_seconds": 199.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.8,
      "end_seconds": 206.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me. It's glimepiride, before breakfast for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.39,
      "end_seconds": 208.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.44,
      "end_seconds": 217.88,
      "duration_seconds": 8.44,
      "text": "2 milligrams. It's paracetamol, 500 milligrams, when needed. I'd been on Glycomet, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.18,
      "end_seconds": 221.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.56,
      "end_seconds": 224.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.16,
      "end_seconds": 230.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.92,
      "end_seconds": 248.0,
      "duration_seconds": 17.08,
      "text": "Well, I've had acid reflux for about ten years now. An underactive thyroid, for nearly five years. My family kept telling me to get it checked. I, I have diabetes, for two years. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.44,
      "end_seconds": 261.16,
      "duration_seconds": 11.72,
      "text": "Yes, I can see the acid reflux in your file as well. Okay, diabetes, that's already on your record. Good to know. Right, do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.78,
      "end_seconds": 266.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.82,
      "end_seconds": 271.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.42,
      "end_seconds": 278.46,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "My father had a heart attack. Yeah, uh, my mother has migraines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.37,
      "end_seconds": 283.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Right, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.29,
      "end_seconds": 285.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.68,
      "end_seconds": 290.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.4,
      "end_seconds": 292.1,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.98,
      "end_seconds": 296.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Tell me if anything hurts as I press."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.87,
      "end_seconds": 313.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Ankle reflexes are absent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.5,
      "end_seconds": 316.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Bear with me a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.19,
      "end_seconds": 329.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Feeling of light touch is reduced in both feet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.28,
      "end_seconds": 359.3,
      "duration_seconds": 25.02,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. Okay, so my impression is this: It fits best with peripheral neuropathy, possibly related to sugar. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. A vitamin B12 deficiency is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 360.43,
      "end_seconds": 362.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.04,
      "end_seconds": 382.19,
      "duration_seconds": 18.15,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like peripheral neuropathy, possibly related to sugar, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had burning in both feet for about a year, severe, and no hand symptoms or back pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 383.79,
      "end_seconds": 385.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 386.25,
      "end_seconds": 389.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.7,
      "end_seconds": 404.61,
      "duration_seconds": 14.91,
      "text": "Not really, um, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 405.93,
      "end_seconds": 432.12,
      "duration_seconds": 26.19,
      "text": "Let's get a nerve conduction study, for neuropathy. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I'd like to arrange a vitamin B12 level for neuropathy. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I'll start you on pregabalin, 75 milligrams, at night, for four weeks. It's for nerve pain. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 433.25,
      "end_seconds": 435.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Alright, I'll pick it up today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 436.32,
      "end_seconds": 451.54,
      "duration_seconds": 15.22,
      "text": "Check your feet every evening for cuts or blisters, you may not feel them. I'll also refer you to podiatry. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 453.02,
      "end_seconds": 455.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Okay, um, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 455.61,
      "end_seconds": 461.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Please don't sit on it if the symptoms get worse. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 462.8,
      "end_seconds": 464.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 465.41,
      "end_seconds": 467.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Come back in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 468.55,
      "end_seconds": 469.25,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0072",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 469.76,
      "end_seconds": 476.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0073",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 476.85,
      "end_seconds": 484.46,
      "duration_seconds": 7.61,
      "text": "So, I take the pregabalin, 75 milligrams, at night and come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0074",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 485.74,
      "end_seconds": 491.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, that's all I have. Is there anything you wanted to ask?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0075",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 492.96,
      "end_seconds": 495.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Hmm, thanks so much, doctor."
    }
  ]
}